<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-14">14 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Second Spanish Republic is proclaimed</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After republicans swept the cities in municipal elections, the Republic was declared and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xiii">Alfonso XIII</a> left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. The new democracy was overthrown by the civil war that began in 1936.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-1">1 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Empire State Building opens in New York</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President Hoover pressed a button in Washington to switch on the lights of the newly finished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skyscraper">skyscraper</a>. At 381 metres it remained the world's tallest building for nearly forty years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/statute-of-westminster-1931">Statute of Westminster 1931</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Statute of Westminster 1931 was an Act of the British Parliament that recognised the legislative independence of the self-governing dominions.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mukden-incident" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mukden-incident.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Crisis</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/mukden-incident">Mukden Incident</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Mukden Incident was a staged explosion on a Japanese-owned railway near Mukden in Manchuria in 1931.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/1931-china-floods" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/1931-china-floods.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/1931-china-floods">1931 China floods</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 1931 China floods were a series of floods from June to August 1931 along the Yangtze and Huai rivers, which struck Wuhan, Nanjing and other cities and culminated in a dike breach along Lake Gaoyou on 25 August.</p></div></li></ol></section>
